    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1081">

                <pb facs="1009" n="751" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg751"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        German Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bernstorff</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-08-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 28, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: I have received your
                    note of the 8th instant, in explanation of the action of the officers of a
                    German torpedo boat in holding up the American steamship <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Muskogee</hi> and <pb facs="1010" n="752" xml:id="pg752"/> the removal from
                    the vessel of two of its seamen, and beg to thank you for your attention to the
                    matter.</p>
                <p>You will appreciate that this Government cannot acquiesce in a practice which
                    might be regarded as lending assistance to deserting seamen from American
                    vessels on the high seas.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
